Title: A Small Law with Exceptions.
Note: Rules with provisos and overrides. The outcome never depends on the order the rules are written in: priority is the transitive closure of the notwithstanding clauses, which must be acyclic, and two maximal rules that disagree are refused, never settled by position.
§1 Let income be 0.
§2 Let resident be true.
§3 Define rate as 20, provided that resident is true.
§4 Define rate as 30, unless resident is true.
§5 Notwithstanding §3, define rate as 10, provided that income is at most 12000 and resident is true.
§6 Notwithstanding §5, define rate as 0, provided that income is at most 4000 and resident is true.
§7 For each step from 0 to 6, do the following.
§7.1 Set income to step times 3000.
§7.2 Say "resident, income " followed by income followed by ": rate " followed by rate.
§8 Set resident to false.
§9 Set income to 3000.
§10 Say "non-resident, income 3000: rate " followed by rate.
